    sections: [
      {
        type: 'about',
        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Rubamazzo',
            subtitle: 'Card game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Rubamazzo (Steal The Pile) is an Italian Scopa-style fishing game. 40-card pack. Capture table cards by matching value or sum. Must capture if possible. Sweep (scopa) = take all from table. Multiple deck styles (Bergamo, Neapolitan, etc.). Fast-paced; strategy and basic math.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Rubamazzo is an Italian Scopa-style fishing game; the name means 'steal the pile' (rubare = to steal, mazzo = deck). Scopa was particularly popular in Naples during the 18th century and was already widespread throughout Italy; it is believed to derive from Spanish games (Primero and Scarabucion) played in Naples' port area as early as the 15th century. As a Scopa variant, Rubamazzo shares this tradition: capture by matching a single card or the sum of table cards, compulsory capture when possible, and scopa (sweep) when clearing the table.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Two or more players.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '40 Italian (or modified 52). A=1, 2-7=face, J=8, Q=9, K=10.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '40-card pack.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '3 each; 4 face up on table.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
